DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _G_e_n_e_r_a_l _n_o_t_e: Most programs should use mutexes instead of  spin  locks.
       Spin  locks are primarily useful in conjunction with real‐time schedul‐
       ing policies.  See NOTES.

       The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() function allocates any resources  required  for
       the  use  of the spin lock referred to by _l_o_c_k and initializes the lock
       to be in the unlocked state.  The _p_s_h_a_r_e_d argument must have one of the
       following values:

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__PPRROOCCEESSSS__PPRRIIVVAATTEE
              The spin lock is to be operated on only by threads in  the  same
              process as the thread that calls pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt().  (Attempt‐
              ing  to  share  the spin lock between processes results in unde‐
              fined behavior.)

       PPTTHHRREEAADD__PPRROOCCEESSSS__SSHHAARREEDD
              The spin lock may be operated on by any thread  in  any  process
              that  has  access  to  the memory containing the lock (i.e., the
              lock may be in a shared memory object that is shared among  mul‐
              tiple processes).

       Calling  pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt()  on a spin lock that has already been ini‐
       tialized results in undefined behavior.

       The pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ddeessttrrooyy() function destroys a  previously  initialized
       spin  lock,  freeing  any  resources that were allocated for that lock.
       Destroying a spin lock that has not been previously been initialized or
       destroying a spin lock while another thread holds the lock  results  in
       undefined behavior.

       Once  a  spin  lock has been destroyed, performing any operation on the
       lock other than once more initializing it with pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt()  re‐
       sults in undefined behavior.

       The  result  of  performing  operations  such  as pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__lloocckk(3),
       pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__uunnlloocckk(3), and pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__ddeessttrrooyy() on _c_o_p_i_e_s of the ob‐
       ject referred to by _l_o_c_k is undefined.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, there functions return zero.  On failure,  they  return  an
       error number.  In the event that pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() fails, the lock is
       not initialized.

EERRRROORRSS
       pptthhrreeaadd__ssppiinn__iinniitt() may fail with the following errors:

       EEAAGGAAIINN The  system  has insufficient resources to initialize a new spin
